From bb0f6c30292612a4797e03dd7dc0a4a08d1fb616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deepx-yjsong <yjsong@deepx.ai>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:14:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix(infer): bound the EOS drain waits

Both EOS drains (per-stream and global) waited without a bound on the
streaming thread. A device that stops completing work pinned the thread
forever, and on the global EOS the pipeline could not shut down.

Add eos-drain-timeout (ns, default 5 s, 0 = unbounded). On expiry the EOS
is forwarded with a WARNING. The backend Put() backpressure wait is left
unbounded on purpose: blocking there is the intended degradation under load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
